### expansions bash parses but rejects when it runs them
#!/bin/bash
echo "${}"
echo "${@word@}"
echo "${!}"
>>> none
>>+ SL2008 2:7 -- shell-lsp native check; bash runs into "bad substitution" here and shellcheck 0.11 does not report it
>>+ SL2008 3:7 -- shell-lsp native check; bash runs into "bad substitution" here and shellcheck 0.11 does not report it

### expansions other checks already explain are not reported twice
#!/bin/bash
x=1
echo "${$x}"
echo "${:-word}"
>>> SC2082 3:7
>>+ SC2034 2:1 -- ${$x} never reads x: bash stops with "bad substitution" before expanding anything
>>+ SC2296 4:9 -- shellcheck 0.11 accepts ${:-word}, which bash rejects with "bad substitution"
